IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lga-concession`
IMPORT `lga-seat`

-- Cases for the pensioner's seat (lga-seat.l4) and the regulative rules of the core (lga-concession.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (act-1993-030.txt, ss 575-584 and the Dictionary;
-- sl-2021-0460.txt, cll 134-136), never copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comment above
-- each. No scenario life raised this Act: the people are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout.
--
-- The main question takes 27 answers, in this order: SSA Chapter 2 payment; VEA Part III service pension; entitled to
-- a pensioner concession card; DVA war widow(er) pension; DVA mother's pension; MRCA s 234(1)(b); within the card's
-- income and assets limits; VEA s 22(4) or s 24 rate; MRCA SRDP; a dwelling on the land; my sole or principal place
-- of living; co-liable spouse living with me (count); co-liable other eligible pensioners (count); co-liable partners
-- of other eligible pensioners (count); other co-liable persons (count); the part liable by me and those with me;
-- ordinary rates; domestic waste charges; water special rates or charges; sewerage special rates or charges; other
-- rates or charges; the rating year; the day the notice was served; the day I became an eligible pensioner; a s 580
-- variation; a s 577 hardship order; a s 582 waiver.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days.

`1 Mar 2016`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2016
`1 Jul 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025
`15 Jul 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 7 2025
`20 Jul 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 7 2025
`21 Jul 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 21 7 2025
`1 Aug 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2025
`30 Sep 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2025
`1 Oct 2025`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025
`10 Nov 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 11 2025
`15 Nov 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 15 11 2025
`31 Dec 2025` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2025
`5 Feb 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 2 2026
`31 Mar 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2026
`1 Apr 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2026
`20 Apr 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 4 2026
`30 Jun 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026
`5 Jul 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 7 2026
`10 Jul 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 10 7 2026
`30 Sep 2010` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 2010

-- Expected answers, written out by hand.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER, `c` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER, `total` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Reduction answer`
`expected reduction` `a` `b` `c` `d` `total` MEANS
    `on application with evidence, reduced by (dollars)`
        (`Reduction` WITH
            `on ordinary rates and domestic waste management charges` IS `a`
            `on water supply special rates or charges`                IS `b`
            `on sewerage special rates or charges`                    IS `c`
            `on other rates or charges`                               IS `d`)
        `total`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. Margaret, 74, on the age pension (SSA Chapter 2, Part 2.2) with a pensioner concession card, sole owner of
-- the house she lives in, in a Sydney Water area (no council water or sewerage rates). HYPOTHETICAL. 2025-26: notice
-- served 15 July 2025; a pensioner since 1 March 2016. Ordinary rates $1,420, domestic waste $560.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- cl 134(a): Chapter 2 payment and entitled to a card.
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cl 134(a): a Social Security Act Chapter 2 pension, benefit or allowance, or a VEA Part III service pension, with entitlement to a pensioner concession card`
-- Dictionary: in a class, and the dwelling is her sole or principal place of living.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible pensioner for the rates on this land` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an eligible pensioner for the rates and charges on this land` `cl 134(a): a Social Security Act Chapter 2 pension, benefit or allowance, or a VEA Part III service pension, with entitlement to a pensioner concession card`
-- Solely liable: s 575(2)(a).
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 575(2) applies to me` 0 0 0 0 1 EQUALS `s 575(2)(a): solely liable, or jointly liable with jointly eligible occupiers and no other person -- one-half`
-- A pensioner (since 2016) on the levy day: the whole year (s 575(2)).
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `15 Jul 2025` `1 Mar 2016` EQUALS `the whole year: an eligible pensioner on the day the rate or charge was levied (s 575(2))`
-- s 575(2)(a), (3)(a): (1,420 + 560) / 2 = 990, capped at $250. Water and sewerage 0. Total $250.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1420 560 0 0 0 2025 `15 Jul 2025` `1 Mar 2016` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 250 0 0 0 250
-- Finding 3: a $25 stormwater management charge is "a rate or charge" halved under s 575(2) and capped by nothing in
-- s 575(3): 12.50 more. Total 250 + 12.50 = $262.50.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1420 560 0 0 25 2025 `15 Jul 2025` `1 Mar 2016` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 250 0 0 12.5 262.5
-- Not covered (s 580): a regulation varying the amounts.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1420 560 0 0 0 2025 `15 Jul 2025` `1 Mar 2016` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `a regulation under s 580 varies the amounts of the reduction; the deposited regulation varies none`
-- Not covered (ss 577-578): a council hardship order.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1420 560 0 0 0 2025 `15 Jul 2025` `1 Mar 2016` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `a council hardship order under ss 577 and 578 applies; its effect and date are the council's`
-- Not covered (s 582, cl 136): a council waiver.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1420 560 0 0 0 2025 `15 Jul 2025` `1 Mar 2016` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `a council waiver or reduction under s 582 and cl 136 applies; its amount is the council's`
-- Not covered (s 546(2)): rates for 2025-26 levied by a notice served on 10 July 2026, in the following year.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1420 560 0 0 0 2025 `10 Jul 2026` `1 Mar 2016` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the rates notice was not served in the rating year it is for (s 546(2), (3))`
-- Margaret's investment unit, which she does not live in: not an eligible pensioner for its rates.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 0 1 900 400 0 0 0 2025 `15 Jul 2025` `1 Mar 2016` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no reduction: not an eligible pensioner` `not an eligible pensioner: does not occupy the dwelling as sole or principal place of living`
-- A vacant lot she owns: no dwelling on the land.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible pensioner for the rates on this land` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not an eligible pensioner: no dwelling (a building or part of one used as a place of dwelling) is situated on the land`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. Ron, on the disability support pension (SSA Chapter 2, Part 2.3) with a pensioner concession card, owns his
-- house in a country town with his wife Jan, who lives with him and is not a pensioner. The council supplies water and
-- sewerage. HYPOTHETICAL. 2025-26: notice served 1 August 2025; a pensioner since 30 September 2010. Ordinary rates
-- $380, domestic waste $90, water $160, sewerage $500.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Jan is his spouse and has the same principal place of living: a jointly eligible occupier (limb (a)).
#ASSERT `Is this other person liable with me a jointly eligible occupier` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Jointly liable only with a jointly eligible occupier: s 575(2)(a), one-half.
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 575(2) applies to me` 1 0 0 0 1 EQUALS `s 575(2)(a): solely liable, or jointly liable with jointly eligible occupiers and no other person -- one-half`
-- (380 + 90) / 2 = 235, under $250. Water 160 / 2 = 80, under $87.50. Sewerage 500 / 2 = 250, capped at $87.50.
-- Total 235 + 80 + 87.50 = $402.50.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 1 0 0 0 1 380 90 160 500 0 2025 `1 Aug 2025` `30 Sep 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 235 80 87.5 0 402.5
-- The part liable is read only under (2)(b): a nonsense part (5) changes nothing under (2)(a).
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 1 0 0 0 5 380 90 160 500 0 2025 `1 Aug 2025` `30 Sep 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 235 80 87.5 0 402.5
-- If Jan had moved out for good (still a co-owner), she would not be a jointly eligible occupier.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this other person liable with me a jointly eligible occupier` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. Dorothy, a war widow on a DVA pension, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits,
-- co-owns her home with her son Paul, who lives elsewhere; as between them each is liable for half. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- 2025-26: notice served 20 July 2025; widowed in 2010. Ordinary $1,700, domestic waste $300, water $200, sewerage $60.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- cl 134(b)(i), with the means test met.
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cl 134(b): a DVA pension as a war widow or widower, or as the mother of a deceased unmarried member, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits`
-- Paul meets no limb and does not live with her: not a jointly eligible occupier; so s 575(2)(b).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this other person liable with me a jointly eligible occupier` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 575(2) applies to me` 0 0 0 1 0.5 EQUALS `s 575(2)(b): jointly liable with a person who is not a jointly eligible occupier -- the proportional share of one-half`
-- s 575(2)(b), (3): ordinary and waste 2,000 / 2 = 1,000, times 0.5 = 500; cap 250 times 0.5 = 125: $125.
-- Water 200 / 2 x 0.5 = 50; cap 87.50 x 0.5 = 43.75: $43.75. Sewerage 60 / 2 x 0.5 = 15, under 43.75: $15.
-- Total 125 + 43.75 + 15 = $183.75.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 1 0.5 1700 300 200 60 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `30 Sep 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 125 43.75 15 0 183.75
-- s 575(5): as between Dorothy and Paul, she is discharged to the extent of the reduction, $183.75. A sole owner has
-- no one to be discharged against: 0.
#ASSERT `the s 575(5) discharge for` (`my liability from` 0 0 0 1 0.5) `of` 183.75 EQUALS 183.75
#ASSERT `the s 575(5) discharge for` (`my liability from` 0 0 0 0 1) `of` 250 EQUALS 0
-- Not covered: a part of 1.2, or of 0, is not a part of the whole.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 1 1.2 1700 300 200 60 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `30 Sep 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the part stated for the applicant and jointly eligible occupiers is not more than 0 and at most 1`
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 1 0 1700 300 200 60 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `30 Sep 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the part stated for the applicant and jointly eligible occupiers is not more than 0 and at most 1`
-- Over the card's income and assets limits: cl 134(b) fails, and she is in no class.
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in no class prescribed by cl 134`
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 1 0.5 1700 300 200 60 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `30 Sep 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no reduction: not an eligible pensioner` `not an eligible pensioner: in no class prescribed by cl 134`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 4. Kevin, on the age pension with a card, and his wife Lyn own three-quarters of their home as between all
-- owners; their daughter Amy, who lives with them and is not a pensioner, owns a quarter. HYPOTHETICAL. 2025-26:
-- notice served 20 July 2025. Ordinary $500, domestic waste $100.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Amy lives there but is not a spouse, not an eligible pensioner and not the partner of one: not a jointly eligible
-- occupier (finding 2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this other person liable with me a jointly eligible occupier` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Lyn (spouse, with him) and Amy (none): s 575(2)(b).
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 575(2) applies to me` 1 0 0 1 0.75 EQUALS `s 575(2)(b): jointly liable with a person who is not a jointly eligible occupier -- the proportional share of one-half`
-- 600 / 2 = 300, times 0.75 = 225; cap 250 x 0.75 = 187.50: $187.50. Total $187.50.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 1 0 0 1 0.75 500 100 0 0 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `30 Sep 2010` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 187.5 0 0 0 187.5
-- Other jointly eligible occupiers: Kevin's sister, an eligible pensioner living with them (limb (b)), and her husband
-- (limb (c)); a spouse and another eligible pensioner together still leave (2)(a).
#ASSERT `Is this other person liable with me a jointly eligible occupier` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this other person liable with me a jointly eligible occupier` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Which paragraph of s 575(2) applies to me` 1 1 1 0 1 EQUALS `s 575(2)(a): solely liable, or jointly liable with jointly eligible occupiers and no other person -- one-half`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. Helen becomes an eligible pensioner part-way through the year: the age pension with a card from
-- 10 November 2025. Sole owner. HYPOTHETICAL. 2025-26: notice served 20 July 2025. Ordinary $1,500, domestic waste
-- $300, sewerage $300 (no council water).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 575(4): the quarters begin 1 Jul, 1 Oct 2025, 1 Jan, 1 Apr 2026; after 10 Nov 2025 two full quarters remain.
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `10 Nov 2025` EQUALS `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` 2
-- Full-year reduction: 1,800 / 2 = 900, capped 250; sewerage 300 / 2 = 150, capped 87.50. Two quarters of four:
-- 250 x 2/4 = 125; 87.50 x 2/4 = 43.75. Total $168.75.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1500 300 0 300 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `10 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 125 0 43.75 0 168.75
-- On the levy day itself: "on the date on which the rate or charge is levied, an eligible pensioner": the whole year.
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `20 Jul 2025` EQUALS `the whole year: an eligible pensioner on the day the rate or charge was levied (s 575(2))`
-- The day after the levy (finding 4): three full quarters (from 1 Oct). 250 x 3/4 = 187.50; 87.50 x 3/4 = 65.625.
-- Total $253.125.
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `21 Jul 2025` EQUALS `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` 3
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1500 300 0 300 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `21 Jul 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 187.5 0 65.625 0 253.125
-- 30 September 2025: the quarter from 1 October is full and after the day: 3. 1 October 2025: that quarter is not
-- after the day: 2. 31 March 2026: 1 (from 1 April). 1 April 2026: none.
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `30 Sep 2025` EQUALS `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` 3
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `1 Oct 2025` EQUALS `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` 2
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `31 Mar 2026` EQUALS `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` 1
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` 0
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 1 1500 300 0 300 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `1 Apr 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no reduction this year: no full quarter of the rating year remained after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))`
-- After the year has ended (5 July 2026): no quarter of 2025-26 remains.
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `5 Jul 2026` EQUALS `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` 0
-- A notice served in the following year is not covered.
#ASSERT `How much of the year counts if I became an eligible pensioner after my rates were levied` 2025 `10 Jul 2026` `10 Nov 2025` EQUALS `not covered: the rates notice was not served in the rating year it is for (s 546(2), (3))`
-- Joan: the disability support pension with a card from 10 November 2025, half-owner with a son who lives elsewhere;
-- Dorothy's rates. Full-year (2)(b) reduction 125, 43.75, 15 (case 3); times 2/4: 62.50, 21.875, 7.50. Total $91.875.
#ASSERT `How much are my rates and charges reduced this year` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 1 0.5 1700 300 200 60 0 2025 `20 Jul 2025` `10 Nov 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `expected reduction` 62.5 21.875 7.5 0 91.875

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 6. Who is, and who is not, in a cl 134 class. HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A self-funded retiree with a Commonwealth seniors health card: no Chapter 2 payment, no pensioner concession card.
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in no class prescribed by cl 134`
-- JobSeeker payment (SSA Chapter 2, Part 2.12) with a health care card but not entitled to a pensioner concession card.
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in no class prescribed by cl 134`
-- A VEA Part III age service pensioner with a card: cl 134(a).
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cl 134(a): a Social Security Act Chapter 2 pension, benefit or allowance, or a VEA Part III service pension, with entitlement to a pensioner concession card`
-- The widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member, within the limits: cl 134(b)(iii).
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cl 134(b): a DVA pension as a war widow or widower, or as the mother of a deceased unmarried member, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits`
-- An MRCA wholly dependent partner on the s 234(1)(b) weekly amount: within the limits, cl 134(b1); over them, none.
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `cl 134(b1): an MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or weekly amount, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits`
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in no class prescribed by cl 134`
-- A veteran on the VEA s 24 special rate: cl 134(c), with no card and no means test.
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `cl 134(c): the VEA s 22(4) extreme disablement rate or the s 24 special rate`
-- A former member once eligible for the MRCA SRDP, not receiving it now: cl 134(d) still (finding 1).
#ASSERT `Which class prescribed by cl 134 am I in` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `cl 134(d): the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension, received now or eligible for at some time`
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible pensioner for the rates on this land` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `an eligible pensioner for the rates and charges on this land` `cl 134(d): the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension, received now or eligible for at some time`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 7. When the concession ends (s 584). HYPOTHETICAL. Quarters as the Dictionary defines them (finding 5).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- A change on 15 November 2025 (in the quarter ending 31 December): the entitlement ceases on 31 December 2025.
#ASSERT `On what day does my concession end` `15 Nov 2025` EQUALS `31 Dec 2025`
-- Paid the year's reduced rates, $1,600, in full: two quarters remain after 31 December (from 1 January and
-- 1 April 2026): 1,600 x 2/4 = $800 credited.
#ASSERT `How much of what I paid is credited when my concession ends` `15 Nov 2025` TRUE 1600 EQUALS `credited to the rates and charges for the rest of the year (s 584(2)), in dollars` 800
-- Not paid in full: s 584(2) gives no credit.
#ASSERT `How much of what I paid is credited when my concession ends` `15 Nov 2025` FALSE 1600 EQUALS `no s 584(2) credit: the year's reduced rates and charges had not been paid in full when the entitlement ceased`
-- A change on 1 July 2025: ceases 30 September 2025; three quarters remain: 1,200 x 3/4 = $900.
#ASSERT `On what day does my concession end` `1 Jul 2025` EQUALS `30 Sep 2025`
#ASSERT `How much of what I paid is credited when my concession ends` `1 Jul 2025` TRUE 1200 EQUALS `credited to the rates and charges for the rest of the year (s 584(2)), in dollars` 900
-- A change on 5 February 2026: ceases 31 March 2026; one quarter remains: 1,000 x 1/4 = $250.
#ASSERT `On what day does my concession end` `5 Feb 2026` EQUALS `31 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `How much of what I paid is credited when my concession ends` `5 Feb 2026` TRUE 1000 EQUALS `credited to the rates and charges for the rest of the year (s 584(2)), in dollars` 250
-- A change on 20 April 2026: ceases 30 June 2026, the end of the year; nothing remains to credit: $0.
#ASSERT `On what day does my concession end` `20 Apr 2026` EQUALS `30 Jun 2026`
#ASSERT `How much of what I paid is credited when my concession ends` `20 Apr 2026` TRUE 1000 EQUALS `credited to the rates and charges for the rest of the year (s 584(2)), in dollars` 0

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 8. Recovery (s 583(2)) and s 582 relief (cl 136). HYPOTHETICAL.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Written off in the ordinary way: the council may not take proceedings to recover it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can the council recover the reduction it wrote off` FALSE FALSE)
-- Written off because of a wilfully false statement in the application: it may.
#ASSERT `Can the council recover the reduction it wrote off` TRUE FALSE
-- Written off for a quarter after the entitlement ceased under s 584 (finding 6): it may.
#ASSERT `Can the council recover the reduction it wrote off` FALSE TRUE
-- s 582 and cl 136: a Chapter 2 pensioner who holds the card is a prescribed person.
#ASSERT `Is the council allowed to waive or reduce my rates under s 582` TRUE TRUE
-- Entitled to the card but not holding it: not prescribed (finding 8).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the council allowed to waive or reduce my rates under s 582` TRUE FALSE)
-- A VEA service pensioner holding a card, with no Chapter 2 payment: an eligible pensioner under cl 134(a), but not a
-- cl 136 prescribed person (finding 8).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the council allowed to waive or reduce my rates under s 582` FALSE TRUE)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Regulative rules (lga-concession.l4). Day 0 is the day each rule starts.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 575(1), 579, 583(1): HYPOTHETICAL council resolution allowing 120 days from the notice. Margaret applies on day 30;
-- the council reduces and writes off on day 45: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 575(1), 579, 583(1) -- on the pensioner's application, the council must reduce the rate or charge and write the reduction off` TRUE (JUST 120)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the eligible pensioner` `apply to the council in the approved form, with evidence enough to calculate the reduction` 30), (EVENT `the council` `reduce the rate or charge` 45), (EVENT `the council` `write off the amount reduced` 45)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- She does not apply within the 120 days: no breach, and nothing is owed (DO ... LEST FULFILLED).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 575(1), 579, 583(1) -- on the pensioner's application, the council must reduce the rate or charge and write the reduction off` TRUE (JUST 120)) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 121)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No time fixed by resolution: an application on day 400 still calls for the reduction; given on day 410: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 575(1), 579, 583(1) -- on the pensioner's application, the council must reduce the rate or charge and write the reduction off` TRUE NOTHING) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the eligible pensioner` `apply to the council in the approved form, with evidence enough to calculate the reduction` 400), (EVENT `the council` `reduce the rate or charge` 410), (EVENT `the council` `write off the amount reduced` 410)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not an eligible pensioner: nothing is owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 575(1), 579, 583(1) -- on the pensioner's application, the council must reduce the rate or charge and write the reduction off` FALSE (JUST 120)) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the council's s 583(1) duty to write off still pending (it reduced but did not write off; the Act sets no period)
#TRACE `s 575(1), 579, 583(1) -- on the pensioner's application, the council must reduce the rate or charge and write the reduction off` TRUE (JUST 120) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the eligible pensioner` DOES `apply to the council in the approved form, with evidence enough to calculate the reduction` AT 30
    PARTY `the council` DOES `reduce the rate or charge` AT 45

-- s 583(2): an ordinary write-off, over the 365 days asked about: no proceedings, fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 583(2) -- the council must not take proceedings to recover an amount written off, unless for a false statement or under s 584` FALSE FALSE 365) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 366)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A wilfully false statement: the council may take proceedings; doing so on day 100 is fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 583(2) -- the council must not take proceedings to recover an amount written off, unless for a false statement or under s 584` TRUE FALSE 365) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the council` `take proceedings to recover the amount written off` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the council, "s 583(2): a council may not take proceedings to recover ..." (proceedings on day 100)
#TRACE `s 583(2) -- the council must not take proceedings to recover an amount written off, unless for a false statement or under s 584` FALSE FALSE 365 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the council` DOES `take proceedings to recover the amount written off` AT 100

-- s 584(2): a change on 15 November 2025, $1,600 paid in full: the council credits $800 (case 7) on day 10: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 584(2) -- the council must credit the prepaid portion when the concession ends` `15 Nov 2025` TRUE 1600) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the council` (`credit the prepaid portion to the rest of the year` 800) 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not paid in full: no credit is owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 584(2) -- the council must credit the prepaid portion when the concession ends` `15 Nov 2025` FALSE 1600) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the credit of $800 still pending (a credit of only $500 does not match)
#TRACE `s 584(2) -- the council must credit the prepaid portion when the concession ends` `15 Nov 2025` TRUE 1600 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the council` DOES `credit the prepaid portion to the rest of the year` 500 AT 10

-- s 579(3): a reduced rate applies and eligibility is verified as prescribed: the council may reduce next year's rate
-- without a fresh application; doing so is fulfilled. Not verified: s 579(3) gives nothing.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 579(3) -- the council may reduce a later rate or charge without a further application` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the council` `reduce a later rate or charge without a further application` 365)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 579(3) -- the council may reduce a later rate or charge without a further application` TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 582: a prescribed person (Chapter 2 payment, holds the card): the council may waive; doing so is fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 582 -- the council may waive or reduce the rates of a person prescribed by cl 136` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the council` `waive or reduce rates, charges and interest` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 582 -- the council may waive or reduce the rates of a person prescribed by cl 136` TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
